-- CA_0167_la_city_by_district_batch_a_2026.sql
-- LA-cities slice, by-district batch A: Alhambra, Carson, Monterey Park. Gives their council districts reachable
-- geometry, adds Monterey Park's elected City Clerk and City Treasurer, and seeds the Nov 3 2026 contests.
--
-- WHY GEOMETRY. All three cities elect by district (the RR/CC precinct layer carries DIV_CITY 1-5 / 1-4 / 1-5), and
-- each had one district row + office + sitting member per district -- but no address could reach them:
--   * Alhambra and Carson: district rows with geo_id "<city>-council-district-N" and NO polygon (mtfcc NULL).
--   * Monterey Park: the city's own 2026 redistricting polygons were already loaded (CC_0023, source
--     monterey_park_gis_council_redistricting_2026) as mtfcc X0001, but the district rows still said G4110.
-- A district race bound to any of these would have been invisible. Alhambra/Carson polygons = the union of each
-- district's precincts in the LA County Registrar-Recorder precinct layer (Political_Boundaries/MapServer/34,
-- DST_CITY AL / CC, DIV_CITY N = District N; read 2026-09-23; seam slivers < 100 m2 dropped; simplified 2e-6 deg) --
-- the CA_0141 Compton/Pomona method. QA: each city's districts cover its TIGER place polygon 0.998-0.999 with
-- overlaps < 1e-8 deg2; POSITIVE CONTROL: the same dissolve for Monterey Park matches the city's own 2026 map at
-- IoU 0.994-0.997, so the precinct file carries 2026 council lines and its district numbering.
--
-- ELECTION METHOD. Alhambra: nominated AND elected by district since Measure V (2020) -- the city clerk's report on the
-- April 27 2026 ordinance: "these offices shall be nominated from and elected by districts." Carson and Monterey Park
-- elect their council by district and their City Clerk / City Treasurer at large.
--
-- MONTEREY PARK CLERK / TREASURER. No such office existed. Created on the city's existing LOCAL_EXEC district, each
-- under its own chamber (the Carson pattern), holders from the city's Terms of Office page (montereypark.ca.gov/912):
-- Maychelle Yee (City Clerk, not a 2026 candidate) and Amy Lee (City Treasurer, on the ballot).
--
-- CONTESTS (each city clerk's list, verified name by name and district by district against the original; Carson's
-- signed notice is a scan, read from the image):
--   Alhambra City Council District 1          2 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   Alhambra City Council District 2          1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Alhambra City Council District 5          3 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Carson City Council District 2            2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Carson City Council District 4            2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Carson City Clerk                         1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Carson City Treasurer                     1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Monterey Park City Council District 1     1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Monterey Park City Council District 5     2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Monterey Park City Clerk                  1 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Monterey Park City Treasurer              1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
-- Uncontested seats stay on the ballot as far as the city record shows (no EC 10229 appointment found: Alhambra D2,
-- Monterey Park D1 / Clerk / Treasurer; Carson Clerk / Treasurer appear on the clerk's 9/15/2026 notice of nominees).
-- Compton and Pomona have nothing beyond the runoffs CA_0141 already seeded (their other seats were decided June 2).
--
-- RACES go on '2026 LA County General' (d91a20ce-557e-4615-a31b-5b2b3df2ed14); primary_party NULL; no party stored.
-- IDEMPOTENT: geofences on (geo_id, mtfcc); district repoint guarded on the old value; fixed ids for new rows.

BEGIN;

